{"ld": 1649, "paper": "SP657", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, to Establish the Commission to Study and Recommend Solutions for Modernizing and Improving the Effectiveness of the Legislature (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "s-stewart-harold", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-baldacci-joseph", "s-bennett-richard", "s-bernard-susan", "h-greenwood-randall", "s-hickman-craig", "h-nutting-robert", "h-salisbury-suzanne"], "committee_code": "SLG", "committee_name": "State and Local Government", "summary": {"text": "This resolve establishes the Blue Ribbon Commission to Study the Operations of the Legislature. The commission consists of 12 members, including 4 Legislators and 8 members of the public who have expertise in public policy, government relations, private business and organized labor. The commission is required to study the existing structure and operations of the Legislature for the purpose of determining its adequacy and effectiveness and identifying changes to the Legislature that could improve efficiency; provide better information to inform decisions; help prioritize legislative activity; develop, implement and coordinate a strategic plan; and reinforce political trust and support in State Government.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0657&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Died On Adjournment", "final_disposition": {"label": "Died On Adjournment", "date": "2026-04-29", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1649)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0657&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-368)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0657&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (S-368)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Senate", "url": "https://legi